## 1. STANDING RULES (apply to everything below)

1. **Preserve first.** New features are additions behind their own navigation entry. Existing behaviour is the default.
2. **Honest status labels.** Every feature in the UI is `working`, `partial`, `simulated`, or `planned`. Simulated data is always labelled "simulated". Nothing simulated may be presented as a measurement.
3. **Judge and Memory gate.** Every calculation, chart, report, and AI-generated answer in this module passes through The Brain, or is labelled UNREVIEWED. Deterministic recomputation outranks model opinion.
4. **Every formula has a source and a test.** Each calculation in Section 4 has a registry record (formula, symbols, units, assumptions, reference) and an automated test against a worked example. Verify formulas against standards or textbooks. Do not trust memory.
5. **Units are first-class.** Every quantity carries a unit. Convert explicitly, and have the Judge reject calculations that mix incompatible units.
6. **No control of real equipment.** This module is **advisory and analytical only**. It never writes to a PLC, robot, actuator, or control system. No such tool may exist in the code. See Section 6.
7. **No fabricated evidence.** Market statistics, ROI ranges, customer names, and benchmarks are shown only with a named source and date, and the user's own inputs always take priority over generic benchmarks.
8. **Tests must run.** Show real test output.

