## 6. SAFETY, SECURITY, AND CLAIMS

- This software is **not a safety system** and does not replace a certified safety assessment (for example under ISO 13849, ISO 10218, ISO/TS 15066, ISO 13855, or IEC 62443). Every calculator that touches safety shows this notice, the standard it follows, its version, and "verify with a qualified engineer".
- **No writes to equipment**, no command channel, no setpoint changes.
- **OT security basics:** gateway connections are read-only and use least privilege; credentials are stored server-side; no plant data goes to external AI services without a visible disclosure and consent; support an **air-gapped or local-only mode** that disables cloud AI. Refer to IEC 62443 concepts (zones and conduits) in the documentation without claiming compliance.
- **No performance claims** ("increases efficiency by X%") in the UI or reports unless computed from the user's own data in that analysis.
- Humanoid and robot features are labelled as **business-case and engineering analysis tools**. Do not imply the app controls or certifies any robot.

